<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?><kml xmlns="http://www.opengis.net/kml/2.2"><Document><name>ILLUSTRATIVE ussf-317 ascent</name><description>RETIMED 2026-11-13 (board): SpaceX ussf317 page now 'targeting Tuesday, November 17 ... four-hour launch window opens at 7:14 p.m. PT' (backup Wed Nov 18 8:54 p.m. PT) = 2026-11-18T03:14:00Z; LL2 NET same (Go, update 'Delayed to NET November 17 PST'). SpaceX timeline unchanged (MECO 2:26, sep 2:29, SES-1 2:36, fairing 2:58). ZLA CARF 11/149-26 (Area A, for the Nov 16 slot) repeats the 11/116-26 polygon, so the 153.56 deg azimuth stands; no NOTAM yet for the Nov 18 03:14Z window. utc shifted by +256740 s; ECEF geometry unchanged.
ILLUSTRATIVE ASCENT ECEF — Falcon 9 USSF-317 (SLC-4E) — NOT OFFICIAL TELEMETRY
NEW 2026-11-12: SpaceX ussf317 page (checked 2026-11-12): &#x27;targeting Saturday, November 14 ... four-hour launch window opens at 7:55 p.m. PT&#x27; (backup Sun Nov 15 7:41 p.m. PT) = 2026-11-15T03:55:00Z; LL2 NET same (Go, window to 07:55Z). Booster 11th flight (B1100 per Next Spaceflight) -&gt; OCISLY.
Loft: FALCON 9 FAMILY SURROGATE, not this flight: altitude &amp; downrange vs time from SpaceX webcast telemetry of Iridium NEXT-7 (F9 Block 5, VSFB SLC-4E, 25 Jul 2018, MECO T+146 s = USSF-317&#x27;s published MECO T+2:26), 9 s running mean; range = integral of horizontal speed x R/(R+h).
Telemetry source: https://github.com/shahar603/Telemetry-Data/tree/master/Iridium%20NEXT%207. Loft rows are identical to the USSF-627 surrogate (same vehicle, pad, azimuth). FILE ENDS AT T+508 s (telemetry end): USSF-317 SECO, orbit and deploy are NOT published (classified USSF mission).
Events (SpaceX ussf317 timeline https://www.spacex.com/launches/ussf317): Max-Q 1:07, MECO 2:26, sep 2:29, SES-1 2:36, fairing 2:58; booster entry 6:06-6:30, landing burn 7:52, landing 8:11.
Azimuth basis: FAA/ZLA CARF NOTAM 11/116-26 (Area A &#x27;SX USSF317 R-6 26-73&#x27;, valid 2026-11-15T03:55Z-08:17Z; 11/094-26 same polygon for Nov 13) far-edge midpoint 32.733N 119.492W from LL2 pad = 153.56 deg; polygon IDENTICAL to USSF-627&#x27;s 11/067-26 Area A. Area B 11/115-26 (https://space-notices.com/notice/notam-ZLA-11%2F116-26). NAVAREA XII 785/26 Area A is a wider polygon, not used.
ASSUMPTION: plane and everything after the Iridium-telemetry loft is borrowed from USSF-627/Starlink Group 15 analogs (LL2: drop zones exact fits with Group 15; possible Starshield). Inclination unpublished.
Velocity = d/dt of interpolated altitude and ground range (Earth-relative). Payload mass/orbit unpublished: loft is the family profile only.
Pad (LL2): 34.632000N -120.611000E. Frame: WGS-84 ECEF, positions km, velocities km/s.
Constant-azimuth rhumb Az=153.56 deg from pad. Velocity ECEF: v_horiz along Az + hdot Up in local ENU.
T0 used: 2026-11-18T03:14:00Z. Re-run with another T0 by shifting utc_iso only; ECEF geometry is Earth-fixed.</description>
